      "content": "those are some solid academic points. i'm curious though, do most historians and legal scholars actually find those arguments convincing, or are they seen as basically just ways to avoid taking responsibility for the actual impact of slavery? like, is there a consensus on whether these legal arguments hold up against the reality of systemic wealth gaps?",
